Alternatives.Alternative:
**A. Direct-worker supervisor contract (chosen).** One support module,
`src/test-support/coordinator.ts` (`LINKS: M-TEST-SUPPORT`), plus its focused test, with the
existing module header, graph summary, and verification scenario made truthful. Plan preflight;
sibling layout; per-worker workspaces; staged direct launch; log draining; one global deadline;
bounded kill and reap; live stream-fault observation; fail-fast cleanup. Pros: non-duplicative
(no reusable contract exists, even though ad-hoc bounded helpers do); it overturns no ruling; it
makes the later concurrency work drivable with direct workers and a coherent failure boundary;
it matches the stated direction; it is one module plus one test at T1. Cons: test-support code,
so no user-visible change and no production capability; it deliberately guarantees only direct
worker PIDs and only a post-exit output snapshot.
